            title: 'Sette e Mezzo',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Sette e Mezzo (Italian for seven and a half) is an Italian comparing card game similar to blackjack. Players compete against the dealer to get as close as possible to 7½ without exceeding it. Popular in Italy (especially at Christmas), Spain (Siete y Media) and Brazil (Sete e Meio).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: Italy (primary); also Spain as Siete y Media and Brazil as Sete e Meio.\nTime Period: Traditional; in Italy played especially around Christmas.\nHistorical Development: Italian comparing card game similar to blackjack; popular in Italy, Spain and Brazil.\nCultural Significance: In Italy traditionally played during Christmas holidays; popular gambling and family game.',
              },
            ],
          },
